      "message": "I implemented this patch with additional mm-\u003emmu_notifier_lock field, which breaks ABI and the breakage is fixed in the next patch by moving mmu_notifier_lock into mmu_notifier_subscriptions.\nBy splitting the patch this way we can merge only this one into android13-5.xx since in there the ABI is not frozen and having a separate mm-\u003emmu_notifier_lock is more efficient and keeps our code closer to upstream.\n\nFixing the ABI this was was much cleaner than what Todd was suggesting (implementing the new field in mm_struct_ext). This is because several places, including drivers, create mm_struct by themselves, so the changes would be more dispersed and vendor drivers would have a problem if they create their own mm_struct.\n",
